Patch 52. After patch 51.

REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET runs in every generated guest load and store on the platforms with the
physical heap offset (Windows, macOS arm64, Android arm64). It compared the address with
0xE0000000 and selected 0x1000 or 0. It now computes the same value with shifts and an add:
addr >> 29 is 0..7, plus 1 is 8 only from 0xE0000000 up, >> 3 gives 1 or 0, << 12 gives the
offset. The rule itself does not change, and PhysicalHostOffset (rex/system/xmemory.h) keeps the
comparison: it is not in the generated code's hot path, and it is the readable statement of the
rule the generated pch is asserted against.

The generated pch now also asserts the macro against PhysicalHostOffset at 0xDFFFFFFF, 0xFFFFFFFF
and 0, next to the existing 0xE0000000. Linux and macOS x86-64 keep offset 0, so their generated
code does not change beyond those asserts.

Test: the new form against the comparison for all 2^32 addresses, once, outside the tree (0
differences); the asserts on every build, the only continuing check of the 0x1000 value. CI's PPC
tests on Windows and macOS arm64 run the macro only below 0xE0000000, where it gives 0.

PGO: the comparison was a counted region, so this changes the control-flow hash of nearly every
generated function on those platforms. An Android profile trained without this patch fails the
build (-Werror=profile-instr-out-of-date); the retrained profile is published with the merge.

Measurement: POCO X7, Android PGO builds of the game at develop f6c54f8; patch 52 at 0fb2c9b, the
base at develop's series up to 51. Each side has its own profile, trained the same afternoon with
the same runs (2026-10-31). fight.txt, fps cap 0, vsync off, A B B A, each run started at battery
32.0 C with cpu7 at 2.3-2.5 GHz. simpleperf stat --per-thread on the guest main thread over the
fight step only, divided by that step's frames:

    run     fight mean  instructions/frame  cycles/frame
    base 1  22.03 ms    51.77 M             51.72 M
    p52 1   19.66 ms    49.04 M             47.49 M
    p52 2   20.86 ms    48.85 M             48.80 M
    base 2  23.10 ms    53.72 M             54.42 M

Means: instructions -7.2 %, cycles -9.3 %, frame 22.57 to 20.26 ms; every patched run is below
every base run on both counters. The two base runs differ by 3.7 % in instructions per frame, so
the percentage is good to about 2 points; the direction is clear. An earlier A B B A with profiles
trained on different days and one throttled run gave +0.9 ms in the fight, with no counters; it
is not comparable.

Mac mini M2, macOS 26.6, Apple clang 17: base f6c54f8 against patch d942d04, each with its own SDK,
mac-arm64-release without PGO, fight.txt, fps cap 0, vsync off, 1280x720, AC power, no thermal
warnings, A B B A. Fight mean: base 7.38 / 7.89 ms, patched 7.20 / 7.09 ms, -6.4 %, good to a few
points (the base runs are 0.51 ms apart); every patched run is below every base run. No hardware
counters. All runs quit by themselves with no fault; guest call bindings pass on both builds with
the check's fix for .cold pieces.

Windows, same comparison, reported by the owner as a summary: fight -1.2 %, within noise; rest
-2.9 %; 8 of 8 runs clean; bindings pass on both builds. Neutral on x86-64, as expected: the
comparison there was already free of branches.

Linux keeps offset 0: develop 6b3e84b with this SDK passes the binding check and fight.txt.

Upstream: not proposed.

--- a/resources/templates/codegen/pch_h.inja
+++ b/resources/templates/codegen/pch_h.inja
@@ -126,7 +126,8 @@
 
 #if REX_PLATFORM_WIN32 || (REX_PLATFORM_MAC && REX_ARCH_ARM64) || \
     (REX_PLATFORM_ANDROID && REX_ARCH_ARM64)
-#define REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET(addr) (((u32)(addr) >= 0xE0000000u) ? 0x1000u : 0u)
+// addr >= 0xE0000000u ? 0x1000u : 0u, without a comparison: the top 3 bits plus 1 reach 8 only there.
+#define REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET(addr) ((((((u32)(addr)) >> 29) + 1u) >> 3) << 12)
 #else
 #define REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET(addr) 0u
 #endif
@@ -136,6 +137,10 @@
 static_assert(REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET(0xE0000000u) ==
                   rex::memory::detail::PhysicalHostOffset(0xE0000000u),
               "REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET disagrees with the SDK: regenerate with this SDK's rexglue");
+static_assert(REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET(0xDFFFFFFFu) == rex::memory::detail::PhysicalHostOffset(0xDFFFFFFFu) &&
+                  REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET(0xFFFFFFFFu) == rex::memory::detail::PhysicalHostOffset(0xFFFFFFFFu) &&
+                  REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET(0u) == rex::memory::detail::PhysicalHostOffset(0u),
+              "REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET disagrees with the SDK at the heap's boundary");
 
 #define REX_RAW_ADDR(x) (base + (u32)(x) + REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET(x))
 
